cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Test Smells: Code and Data Release"
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite the accompanying paper."
type: dataset
license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
date-released: 2026-05-23
abstract: >-
  A 258-template bank of evaluation cues ("test smells") extracted from six
  widely used LLM benchmarks, along with paired forward-injection and
  preservation-gated reverse-removal datasets, white-box activation probes
  on four open-weight Qwen models, and the full analysis pipeline that
  produced every number in the accompanying EMNLP 2026 submission.
authors:
  - family-names: "Anonymous EMNLP submission"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - evaluation awareness
  - benchmark contamination
  - causal probing
  - safety evaluation
preferred-citation:
  type: conference-paper
  title: >-
    Test Smells: A Causal Decomposition of Eval-Identifiability in Modern LLM
    Benchmarks
  authors:
    - family-names: "Anonymous EMNLP submission"
  year: 2026
  notes: "Under double-blind review; citation will be updated after acceptance."
